    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="1709" n="1693" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">700.022/2–2151</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Second Secretary of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tebbit</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Assistant
                        Legal Adviser for European Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yingling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-02-21">21st February,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Ref. 1271/17/51</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Yingling</hi>: In confirmation of the
                    message which I have already passed to you by telephone, I write to inform you
                    that the Foreign Office are pleased to accept your suggestion that the talks
                    about Territorial Waters should be held during the period March 22nd to March
                    27th inclusive. Sir Eric Beckett, Professor Waldock and Mr. Hanna are making
                    their travel arrangements accordingly.</p>
                <p>2. May I take it that, unless I hear from you to the contrary, the talks can
                    begin on the morning of Thursday March 22nd?<anchor n="1" xml:id="d758-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tebbit</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d758-f1" n="1" xml:id="d758-f1-content">
                <p>Confirmation was sent by Yingling in a letter of February 26.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
